// The workspace worker protocol (RFC GW §8). Internal: not part of the public
// API, not in the adapters, and served only on the worker endpoint, beside the
// conversion worker protocol (proto/worker.proto), never on the public gRPC
// port.
//
// Workers dial the core; the core never dials a worker. A worker holds one
// Attach stream per core (its registration, heartbeats and the core's control
// messages) and a pool of idle Op streams. An Op stream carries exactly one op
// and then ends.
//
// An op names a workspace by its id and carries its arguments as JSON, so a
